# Canonical names for the six members, so `git shortlog -sn` reads like the roster in
# CONTRIBUTIONS.md. This changes how git DISPLAYS authors; it rewrites no commit.
#
# Honoured by `git shortlog` and by the %aN / %aE log placeholders. Ignored by the raw
# %an / %ae placeholders, and by GitHub's contributor graph, which credits by the email
# on the commit.
#
# Huang Yu's two commits carry `huangyu@huangyudeMacBook-Air.local`, git's username@hostname
# fallback when user.email is unset. Once her git email is set to the one on her GitHub
# account, change her line below to `Huang Yu <that address> <huangyu@huangyudeMacBook-Air.local>`
# so both sets of commits count as one person.

